{"availability":"available","full":"AidanBlackmore/INF2573-Group-4","name":"INF2573-Group-4","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T22:04:21Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:36:50Z","branch":"claude/lucid-heisenberg-cgg0ll","homepage":"https://inf-2573-group-4.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://inf-2573-group-4.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:00.236Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:00.236Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:00.236Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:00.236Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Jackbox-style party game: one shared screen on a TV, phones as controllers. Pick one of four universes on the shared screen. Each universe is a pre-written episode in four acts. There is no AI yet.","Phones and the laptop never talk to each other directly. Every action goes to Supabase, and Supabase Realtime tells each screen when something changed. Each screen then reloads the current state from the database. That is also how a phone recovers after a refresh or after the screen locks."],"features":["/host: the shared screen. Open it on a laptop connected to the TV.","/play/CODE: the phone controller. Players get there by scanning the QR code or typing the room code on the home page.","The repo root is the current game (Next.js + Supabase). This is what runs and what Vercel deploys.","research/: interview transcripts, interview synthesis, opportunity solution tree and product brainstorming.","legacy/express-ai-gm/: the earlier Express + Socket.io version with the AI Game Master, casting quiz and secret chapters. Archived as-is, with its own README for running it."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AidanBlackmore/INF2573-Group-4/blob/claude%2Flucid-heisenberg-cgg0ll/README.md","fingerprint":"395232b0d47d2bc6cf6b815dff7bddd0c93252fa4c4f72fe3034c3417b3315